Datiscum Linux 6.18.40
======================

This branch is based on the official Linux v6.18.40 tag and carries the
kernel changes used by the datiscum systems.  The changes are split into
separate Git commits so that every patch group can be audited or replaced by
its stable upstream equivalent in later kernel releases.

Scheduler stability
-------------------

The scheduler series contains the upstream fair-scheduler overflow fixes:

* 4823725d9d1d ("sched/fair: Increase weight bits for avg_vruntime")
* 556146ce5e94 ("sched/fair: Avoid overflow in enqueue_entity()")
* 416dd8fc352b ("sched/fair: Fix overflow in vruntime_eligible()")

It also contains the datiscum-specific defensive check in avg_vruntime():

	if (unlikely(weight <= 0))
		delta = curr ? entity_key(cfs_rq, curr) : 0;

The fallback prevents a zero or negative divisor after inconsistent or
wrapped weight accounting.  It deliberately continues through
update_zero_vruntime(), avoiding both a divide-by-zero panic and an invalid
vruntime jump.

This fixes the scheduler failure path observed before these patches.  That
failure could result in a kernel panic, soft or hard lockups, RCU stalls, or
tasks no longer receiving CPU time.  The fix is particularly relevant to
heavily parallel hosts with many CPU cores, where scheduler failures have a
large system-wide impact.  It addresses this specific accounting failure; it
is not a claim to fix unrelated causes of lockups or RCU stalls.

The affected production machine is a 96-core AMD EPYC system.  Before the
scheduler patches it exhibited the failures described above; with the patched
kernel it has operated stably without those scheduler crashes and lockups.
This is the observed result on that system rather than a general guarantee
for unrelated hardware or failure paths.

The scheduler series additionally prevents try_steal_cookie() from migrating
an rq->donor task that is still the active proxy-execution context.

Intel Xe stability
------------------

The Xe changes are kept in three reviewable groups:

* TTM and Xe buffer-object eviction, execution recovery, GuC register, and
  page-table error-path fixes.
* D3Cold is disabled by default for Battlemage devices to retain the stable
  power-management behavior previously obtained through power/control=on.
* Additional upstream fixes for the GuC steered-register allocation, purged
  BO cursors, BO-prefetch bounds, imported dma-buf lifetime, LNL/Battlemage
  WOPCM sizing, page-table retry state, scheduler timeline-name lifetime, and
  GT resume failures.

The additional Xe group carries upstream commits 24f60b8e9f44,
632ecc90e1ca, 8a0fb57675be, 7bc597ce74ba, 62775525a27c, ad87e2476b3b,
6384271ac1ac, 299bc6d50b1b, and 644673a69f2b, adapted to the Linux 6.18
interfaces without importing later multi-queue interfaces.

Other changes and configuration
-------------------------------

The branch also carries the selected builddeb, Cachy, crypto, and NTFS-Plus
changes.  NTFS-Plus is imported from namjaejeon/linux-ntfs commit
ca149db6b901a0d44cdd88e54047e0cd422ca70d.

The exact build configuration is stored as:

	arch/x86/configs/datiscum_defconfig

Important settings include CONFIG_DRM_XE=m, CONFIG_NTFS_FS=m,
CONFIG_NTFS_FS_POSIX_ACL=y, CONFIG_NTFS3_FS=m, and the local version suffix
"-datiscum1".

Validation
----------

The complete patch series was applied without rejects to a clean v6.18.40
tree.  The resulting source files were compared byte-for-byte with the
previously prepared local Linux 6.18.40 tree.  The only subsequent source
cleanup removed two trailing blank lines reported by git diff --check.  No
kernel compilation was run as part of this repository import.
